(6508737, 967100, 116575, '<td valign="top">a work of art... the black and white is really deep. I especially like the white line in the front because it is not perfectly straight and therefor not perfect like everyone of us. Except everyone of us is different <i>and</i> perfect in their own way, like that line. The texture, focus, and DOF is also extremely nice.<br/>The name signifies not only a physical meaning, but a very spiritual meaning also. What if the was <i>actually</i> no tomorrow? What would you do knowing that everything you did wouldn''t matter in the future. <br/>All in all, the is the most beautiful, deep, and technically <i>perfect</i> photo I have ever seen on this site, no the internet, no the WORLD.<br/>Thank you so much for sharing this with me.<br/>Nicky</td>', 'a work of art... the black and white is really deep. I especially like the white line in the front because it is not perfectly straight and therefor not perfect like everyone of us. Except everyone of us is different and perfect in their own way, like that line. The texture, focus, and DOF is also extremely nice.The name signifies not only a physical meaning, but a very spiritual meaning also. What if the was actually no tomorrow? What would you do knowing that everything you did wouldn''t matter in the future. All in all, the is the most beautiful, deep, and technically perfect photo I have ever seen on this site, no the internet, no the WORLD.Thank you so much for sharing this with me.Nicky', '2011-08-19 00:24:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6508787, 967722, 106233, '<td valign="top">Beautiful picture!</td>', 'Beautiful picture!', '2011-08-19 00:49:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6508796, 967769, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is really quirky and cool.  Love the blur.  Perfect title.  It has a painterly quality to it.  Nice. 7</td>', 'This is really quirky and cool.  Love the blur.  Perfect title.  It has a painterly quality to it.  Nice. 7', '2011-08-19 00:58:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6508879, 967798, 117706, '<td valign="top">woody time eh? ;)</td>', 'woody time eh? ;)', '2011-08-19 01:27:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509007, 967809, 108580, '<td valign="top">Relevant in current times. Where''d you get the old hands: both of them! Well executed yet pocket watch face a bit OE.</td>', 'Relevant in current times. Where''d you get the old hands: both of them! Well executed yet pocket watch face a bit OE.', '2011-08-19 02:49:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509078, 967594, 108580, '<td valign="top">Brave for a simple challenge topic that implies a picture of a watch is what should be photographed. Good one!</td>', 'Brave for a simple challenge topic that implies a picture of a watch is what should be photographed. Good one!', '2011-08-19 04:02:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509083, 967155, 108580, '<td valign="top">But it''s not a picture of a clock! Can''t possibly be time related!<br/>LOL. WD in capturing a moment in time :)</td>', 'But it''s not a picture of a clock! Can''t possibly be time related!LOL. WD in capturing a moment in time :)', '2011-08-19 04:04:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509090, 967804, 108580, '<td valign="top">I''ve never liked this style of image. It appears a lot on DPC in various guises and maybe shoehorns. There are really only a few togs who do it here :) <br/>It''s a brave style as DPC is all about crisp, over-saturated, sharp wine glasses on a mirror or water drops with gelled speedlights (exaggeration but I''m making a point) and images that, as in this case, are deemed to be without a doubt supposed to be unequivocally a "time" piece, i.e. a watch or wall clock...<br/>In THIS instance your "imagery" has touched a nerve with me. Not only have you used a slow s/s but the camera shake has also rotated/zoomed the final shot. The dogs on a leash looking into the black worm hole in the shrubbery. It all blends to make a dreamlike remembrance of a moment, passage, of time.<br/> <br/>It''s commendable, and whilst I am guessing you''re getting hammered by the lemming "it''s not a watch" voters, this is the highest mark I''ve given to this style of work ever. WD and bravo.</td>', 'I''ve never liked this style of image. It appears a lot on DPC in various guises and maybe shoehorns. There are really only a few togs who do it here :) It''s a brave style as DPC is all about crisp, over-saturated, sharp wine glasses on a mirror or water drops with gelled speedlights (exaggeration but I''m making a point) and images that, as in this case, are deemed to be without a doubt supposed to be unequivocally a "time" piece, i.e. a watch or wall clock...In THIS instance your "imagery" has touched a nerve with me. Not only have you used a slow s/s but the camera shake has also rotated/zoomed the final shot. The dogs on a leash looking into the black worm hole in the shrubbery. It all blends to make a dreamlike remembrance of a moment, passage, of time. It''s commendable, and whilst I am guessing you''re getting hammered by the lemming "it''s not a watch" voters, this is the highest mark I''ve given to this style of work ever. WD and bravo.', '2011-08-19 04:13:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509093, 967322, 108580, '<td valign="top">Good idea but execution seems hasty. Focus is just not crisp enough for a studio shot (for me). Composition is peculiar, it feels odd to me. I understand the empty house concept and last set of bags. Just the sugar/ashes urn and clock on the suitcase are odd as well.</td>', 'Good idea but execution seems hasty. Focus is just not crisp enough for a studio shot (for me). Composition is peculiar, it feels odd to me. I understand the empty house concept and last set of bags. Just the sugar/ashes urn and clock on the suitcase are odd as well.', '2011-08-19 04:15:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509095, 967047, 108580, '<td valign="top">Hope you are getting decent votes and comments seeing as it is quite obviously not a watch or grandfather clock! lol.<br/>Great period style image worthy of publication. Without a doubt DMC.<br/>High marks.</td>', 'Hope you are getting decent votes and comments seeing as it is quite obviously not a watch or grandfather clock! lol.Great period style image worthy of publication. Without a doubt DMC.High marks.', '2011-08-19 04:17:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509097, 967270, 108580, '<td valign="top">Weird but certainly DMC. You''re getting nailed right?<br/>I''m not fond of this style but it certainly has a Hitchcock feel.<br/>Brave entry.</td>', 'Weird but certainly DMC. You''re getting nailed right?I''m not fond of this style but it certainly has a Hitchcock feel.Brave entry.', '2011-08-19 04:19:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509098, 967601, 108580, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot and brave entry. Sure it''s a timeless antique piece and I have been very open minded to this challenges entries but this one just doesn''t give me a solid connection other than it''s an antique.</td>', 'Beautiful shot and brave entry. Sure it''s a timeless antique piece and I have been very open minded to this challenges entries but this one just doesn''t give me a solid connection other than it''s an antique.', '2011-08-19 04:21:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509101, 967760, 108580, '<td valign="top">Super and relevant. WD. Lovely candid.</td>', 'Super and relevant. WD. Lovely candid.', '2011-08-19 04:23:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509102, 967242, 108580, '<td valign="top">Decay. Hope others get it too...brave entry.</td>', 'Decay. Hope others get it too...brave entry.', '2011-08-19 04:23:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509105, 967797, 108580, '<td valign="top">Gutsy entry. I get it. Do others? Oh wait it''s not a picture of Granddads pocket watch. Mark it down mark it down!<br/>I didn''t. Love the B&amp;W and upside down composition implying death, wilting, end of its time.</td>', 'Gutsy entry. I get it. Do others? Oh wait it''s not a picture of Granddads pocket watch. Mark it down mark it down!I didn''t. Love the B&W and upside down composition implying death, wilting, end of its time.', '2011-08-19 04:25:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509108, 967663, 108580, '<td valign="top">Valid entry. His timing has to be perfect to stay upright. You have to get your timing and s/s to get the shot. I fear that is a bit off, even with slight panning. There''s fuzziness, blur in the water and foam floating and it''s making my eyes water. Whilst the surfer is fairly stop motion, I am still getting woozy. Not bad, just a bit off.</td>', 'Valid entry. His timing has to be perfect to stay upright. You have to get your timing and s/s to get the shot. I fear that is a bit off, even with slight panning. There''s fuzziness, blur in the water and foam floating and it''s making my eyes water. Whilst the surfer is fairly stop motion, I am still getting woozy. Not bad, just a bit off.', '2011-08-19 04:27:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509109, 967794, 108580, '<td valign="top">Love it. DMC. Well spotted. Great backlighting.</td>', 'Love it. DMC. Well spotted. Great backlighting.', '2011-08-19 04:27:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509110, 967759, 108580, '<td valign="top">One of the few "photo of a watch" entries I actually liked in this challenge.<br/>I love the motion in the second hand and the blur in the red tip. Technically the big hand should be between minute 59 and 60 and not ON 59 as it is here seeing as the seconds are so close to the end of the minute.<br/>Otherwise a nice simple and effective image not overly processed.</td>', 'One of the few "photo of a watch" entries I actually liked in this challenge.I love the motion in the second hand and the blur in the red tip. Technically the big hand should be between minute 59 and 60 and not ON 59 as it is here seeing as the seconds are so close to the end of the minute.Otherwise a nice simple and effective image not overly processed.', '2011-08-19 04:30:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509112, 967132, 108580, '<td valign="top">This will do well and is fun. I''m a bit stumped as to why Frog''s front "fingers" are turned unnaturally inwards?</td>', 'This will do well and is fun. I''m a bit stumped as to why Frog''s front "fingers" are turned unnaturally inwards?', '2011-08-19 04:32:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6509131, 967707, 108580, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image. Perfect timing. Great basic BW PP. Not overly processed as it is basic editing. Natural and as it was. The concept of timing to get a landscape shot seems lost in this challenge. At a guess this is a Hahn.</td>', 'Beautiful image. Perfect timing. Great basic BW PP. Not overly processed as it is basic editing. Natural and as it was. The concept of timing to get a landscape shot seems lost in this challenge. At a guess this is a Hahn.', '2011-08-19 05:22:03.000000', NULL, 1),
